posts.body:
VisuStella.
I am NOT an expert.  I've been playing with the allowed formulas and pulling my hair out.  The formulas I'm using now are shown below:
Initial Speed
= Math.random() * 5
-----------------------------
let speed =
((user.agi +100)/20) + 5;
const user = this;
----------------------------------
let speed =
((baseAgility +100)/20) + 5;
const user = this;
const baseAgility = user.paramBasePlus(6);
----------------------------------
let relativeSpeed =
speed / partyBaseSpeed;
const user = this;
const speed = user.tpbSpeed()
const partyBaseSpeed = $gameParty.tpbBaseSpeed();
------------------------------------
let acceleration =
speed / referenceTime;
const user = this;
const speed = user.tpbRelativeSpeed();
const referenceTime = $gameParty.tpbReferenceTime();
------------------------------------
let time =
delay / 100;
const user = this;
const actions = user._actions.filter(action => action.isValid());
const items = actions.map(action => action.item());
const delay = items.reduce((r, item) => r + Math.max(0, -item.speed), 0);
---------------------------------------
original CAST TIME FORMULA:  let time = delay / user.tpbSpeed();
CHANGED TO:
let time = delay / 100
My Cast time formula makes it so that -1 skill speed is a 1% of a turn delay, so -100 makes you wait a turn till it activates, then another turn yet before you can act.
I don't know how to make the code read a stat other than the Agility.  It seems like LUK would make sense for start of battle order.  I do not even know what the initiative (start of combat) formula is actually doing.  I would like to see CTB completely redone, but I can't find another plugin that works any better.  After fiddling more, here are the skill settings to use for approximate desired turn speeds:
0% turn duration  =  +2000ss  +skilltag  <CTB After Speed: 100%>
20% turn duration  =  +2000ss  +skilltag  <CTB After Speed: 80%>
40% turn duration  =  +2000 skill speed
60% turn duration  =  +1400 skill speed
80% turn duration  =  +700   skill speed
100% turn duration  =   (no change)
120% turn duration  =  -20 skill speed
140% turn duration  =  -40 skill speed
160% turn duration  =  -60 skill speed
180% turn duration  =  -80 skill speed
200% turn duration  =  -100 skill speed
